Thinking: We need to answer user question: "How do I load a .pmtiles file as a source in MapLibre GL JS?" Provide step-by-step instructions, include installing pmtiles library, registering protocol, using style source with url pmtiles://..., mention MapLibre version changes, ensure correct addProtocol usage, CORS, hosting, example code. Also mention using raster vs vector, using TileJSON, using url not tiles, etc. Provide full answer.

Below is a complete, copy‑and‑paste‑ready recipe for loading a **single‑file PMTiles archive** (vector, raster or raster‑DEM) into a MapLibre GL JS map.

---

## 1️⃣ Install the PMTiles helper library

MapLibre itself does not understand the `pmtiles://` protocol.  
The tiny **pmtiles** npm package adds a protocol handler that knows how to do HTTP Range requests and return the right tile data.

```bash
# From your project root
npm install pmtiles
# (or yarn add pmtiles, pnpm add pmtiles)
```

> **Tip:** The library works in the browser (ES‑modules) and in Node‑based bundlers (Vite, Webpack, Next.js, etc.).

---

## 2️⃣ Register the protocol **once** before any map is created

```js
// src/pmtiles-setup.js  (or any file that runs at app start)
import * as pmtiles from 'pmtiles';
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';

// Create the protocol instance
const pmtilesProtocol = new pmtiles.Protocol();

// Register it with MapLibre
//   - The first argument is the scheme name you will use in the style (`pmtiles`)
//   - The second argument is the handler function (`protocol.tile`)
//   - This works for MapLibre GL JS ≥ v3 and the newer promise‑based v4+ API.
maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', pmtilesProtocol.tile);

// Optional clean‑up (e.g. in a React useEffect return)
// maplibregl.removeProtocol('pmtiles');
```

> **Why register only once?**  
> `addProtocol` stores the handler in a global registry. Registering it a second time throws an error, and registering inside a component that mounts/unmounts repeatedly can leak abort controllers. Put the call in a top‑level module, a root‑level React effect, or a simple script tag that runs before you create the map.

---

## 3️⃣ Prepare a style that points at the PMTiles file

### 3.1 Vector tiles (most common)

```js
// src/map.js
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

// The style can be an inline object (as below) or a separate JSON file.
const style = {
  version: 8,
  sources: {
    // One source per PMTiles file
    world: {
      type: 'vector',
      // NOTE: use the `url` property, **not** `tiles: []`.
      // The protocol handler reads the archive header and returns a TileJSON
      // with the correct minzoom / maxzoom, bounds, etc.
      url: 'pmtiles://https://my-cdn.example.com/basemap.pmtiles'
    }
  },
  layers: [
    // Background (optional)
    {
      id: 'bg',
      type: 'background',
      paint: { 'background-color': '#f8f4f0' }
    },
    // Water (example layer)
    {
      id: 'water',
      type: 'fill',
      source: 'world',
      'source-layer': 'water',          // name of the vector layer inside the PMTiles
      paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' }
    },
    // Roads
    {
      id: 'roads',
      type: 'line',
      source: 'world',
      'source-layer': 'road',
      paint: {
        'line-color': '#777',
        'line-width': [
          'interpolate', ['linear'], ['zoom'],
          5, 0.5,
          12, 2,
          18, 8
        ]
      }
    },
    // Labels (requires glyphs & sprite – see maplibre-source-wiring)
    {
      id: 'place-labels',
      type: 'symbol',
      source: 'world',
      'source-layer': 'place',
      layout: {
        'text-field': ['get', 'name'],
        'text-size': 12,
        'text-font': ['Open Sans Regular', 'Arial Unicode MS Regular']
      },
      paint: {
        'text-color': '#222'
      }
    }
  ]
};

const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',          // <div id="map"></div> in your HTML
  style,                     // the object defined above
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});
```

### 3.2 Raster tiles (imagery)

```json
{
  "type": "raster",
  "url": "pmtiles://https://my-cdn.example.com/satellite.pmtiles",
  "tileSize": 256,
  "maxzoom": 14   // optional – will be read from the archive header if omitted
}
```

Add a layer that uses it:

```js
{
  id: 'satellite',
  type: 'raster',
  source: 'sat',
  paint: { 'raster-opacity': 0.9 }
}
```

### 3.3 Raster‑DEM (terrain)

```json
{
  "type": "raster-dem",
  "url": "pmtiles://https://my-cdn.example.com/elevation.pmtiles",
  "encoding": "terrarium"   // or "mapbox"
}
```

Then enable terrain in the style:

```js
{
  "terrain": {
    "source": "elevation",
    "exaggeration": 1.5
  }
}
```

