## 6️⃣ Common Pitfalls & How to Fix Them

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **Blank tiles / “no data”** | Used `tiles: ['pmtiles://…/{z}/{x}/{y}']` instead of `url:` | Switch to `url:` so the protocol can read the archive header and supply the correct TileJSON. |
| **`addProtocol` callback never resolves** (MapLibre v4+) | Used the old v3 signature (`(params, callback)`) | Use the promise‑based signature (`async (params, abort) => { … return {data}`) **or** keep the one‑liner `maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', protocol.tile)` which already contains a compatibility shim. |
| **CORS error** | Host does not send `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` or `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Range` | Add those headers on the static host or CDN. |
| **404 on tile request** | The URL points to a non‑existent file or the file is behind authentication | Verify the URL works directly in the browser (e.g. `curl -I -H "Range: bytes=0-0" https://…/file.pmtiles`). |
| **Very slow first load** | The whole `.pmtiles` file is being downloaded (no range support) | Ensure the server returns `Accept-Ranges: bytes`. |
| **Zoom levels beyond the archive are missing** | You used `tiles:` and omitted `maxzoom` → MapLibre assumes 22 and keeps requesting higher zooms | Use `url:` (the protocol reads `maxzoom` from the archive) or manually set `maxzoom` in the source if you must use `tiles:`. |
| **Multiple PMTiles files needed** | The dataset is too large for a single file (e.g. global raster at high zoom) | Split the data into regional files and add multiple sources, each with its own `url`. You can also use `pmtiles extract` to create a smaller subset. |

