## 8️⃣ TL;DR – One‑liner for a vector PMTiles source

```js
import * as pmtiles from 'pmtiles';
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';

// Register handler (do this once)
maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', new pmtiles.Protocol().tile);

// Create map
new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {
      mytiles: {
        type: 'vector',
        url: 'pmtiles://https://cdn.example.com/mytiles.pmtiles'
      }
    },
    layers: [
      {
        id: 'water',
        type: 'fill',
        source: 'mytiles',
        'source-layer': 'water',
        paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' }
      }
    ]
  },
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});
```

That’s it—your map now pulls vector (or raster) tiles directly from a single `.pmtiles` file without any tile server! 🎉

